@anon.152f57749fcdf0a673d809c4f4545e7f.619 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [894 x i8] }> <{ [894 x i8] c"If `{true}`, the spacing collapses at the start or end of a paragraph.\0AMoreover, from multiple adjacent weak spacings all but the largest one\0Acollapse.\0A\0AWeak spacing in markup also causes all adjacent markup spaces to be\0Aremoved, regardless of the amount of spacing inserted. To force a space\0Anext to weak spacing, you can explicitly write `[#\22 \22]` (for a normal\0Aspace) or `[~]` (for a non-breaking space). The latter can be useful to\0Acreate a construct that always attaches to the preceding word with one\0Anon-breaking space, independently of whether a markup space existed in\0Afront or not.\0A\0A```example\0A#h(1cm, weak: true)\0AWe identified a group of _weak_\0Aspecimens that fail to manifest\0Ain most cases. However, when\0A#h(8pt, weak: true) supported\0A#h(8pt, weak: true) on both sides,\0Athey do show up.\0A\0AFurther #h(0pt, weak: true) more,\0Aeven the smallest of them swallow\0Aadjacent markup spaces.\0A```" }>, align 1
